{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>And Esav said in his heart.</b> The way of the Sages, may their memory be for a blessing: the wicked are in the power of their heart — (Psalms 14:1) ״אמר נבל בלבו״, (Genesis 27) ״ויאמר עשו בלבו״, (I Kings 12:26) ״ויאמר ירבעם בלבו״; but the righteous — their heart is in their power: (I Samuel 1:13) ״וחנה היא מדברת על לבה״, (ibid. 27:1) ״ויאמר דוד אל לבו״, (Daniel 1:8) ״וישם דניאל על לבו״. They resemble their Creator: (Genesis 8:21) ״ויאמר ה' אל לבו״." "<b>The days of mourning for my father draw near.</b> He did not wish to kill him during his father's lifetime, for he feared in his soul lest he curse him and the blessing turn back upon him as a curse; and since Yaakov hid away out of fear of Esav and went outside the city, therefore Rivkah needed to send for him to the place where he was."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:15:40.921166842Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}